326	#[derive(Default)]
327	struct State {
328	    /// Conversions by (type handle, depth), each entry with the enclosing instantiations it depended on. The handles
329	    /// are valid inside this snapshot only.
330	    ///
331	    /// Why an entry may be reused where [`Entry::holds_in`] says. A conversion reads its context in two ways only: the
332	    /// depth, which is in the key, and [`Cx::encloses`], the question whether a handle is an instantiation being
333	    /// expanded around the type. Everything else it reads is the checker's answer about the type, which does not change
334	    /// inside a snapshot. So a conversion is a deterministic walk whose every step is fixed by the type, the depth and
335	    /// the answers to those questions, in the order they are asked. Run it again where each handle it asked about has
336	    /// the same answer, and it asks the same questions in the same order and returns the same type. A handle that the
337	    /// conversion opened itself is settled inside it (it was found not to enclose the type at its own gate, which is
338	    /// recorded), so only the handles asked of the outer context are kept. A type in no cycle with its context asks
339	    /// nothing that encloses it and holds everywhere; one in a cycle holds where the same part of the cycle encloses
340	    /// it. Entries that hold in a context all agree, so which of them is found first, and so the order in which
341	    /// types were first reached, cannot show in the output.
342	    memo: Memo,
343	    origins: Mutex<FxHashMap<(bool, CompactSymbol), Option<Origin>>>,
344	    /// By (type handle, whether printed expanded: see [`Rpc::type_to_string_expanded`]).
345	    printed: Mutex<FxHashMap<(u64, bool), String>>,
346	    /// The parts of a type by its handle (see [`Parts`]). They are the checker's answer about the type, fixed inside the
347	    /// snapshot, while the memo converts a type again at another depth or under other instantiations: kept, that
348	    /// conversion asks for none of them again. Kept for the whole snapshot, since components of one library share
349	    /// most of their types: kept per component, a program of every Chakra component answered 16 at a time held 16
350	    /// copies of the same style props' members.
351	    parts: PartsSeen,
352	    /// Where props are declared ([`crate::declared`]), kept for the snapshot like the rest.
353	    declared: crate::declared::Memo,
354	    hits: AtomicU64,
355	    misses: AtomicU64,
356	}
